<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to keep monthly devaluation at 1.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary to keep monthly devaluation at 1.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hungarian government said on Thursday that it would continue to devalue its forint by a maximum monthly rate of 1.2 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>The current monthly rate is 1.2 percent.</p>
<p>Government spokesman Elemer Kiss, announcing the decision, said that the government would examine again in 1997 whether the devaluation rate should be reduced.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom ++ 36 1 327 4040</p>
